      "one_line": "Ship every change the same way: Every change goes from opening to merge through the same steps, with an outside review and a person's yes.",
      "doc": "software-delivery-planning/ship-every-change/capability.md",
      "identified_by": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "fn-731",
      "kind": "feature",
      "mode": "update",
      "one_line": "A person names the change, and its issue is found or filed, its branch is cut from the branch it will land on, and its working folder is made."
    },
    {
      "id": "fn-commit-by-concern",
      "kind": "feature",
      "mode": "new",
      "slug": "fn-commit-by-concern",
      "capability": "cap-ship-every-change",
      "intents": [
        "bi-8"
      ],
      "one_line": "Every changed file is committed on the change's branch in commits of one concern each, each naming its issue, and a sensitive file stops the commit.",
      "doc": "software-delivery-planning/ship-every-change/fn-commit-by-concern/feature.md",
      "identified_by": ""
    },
